  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration found is config_045 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) at 0.7250 accuracy. All four aggregation×fusion combinations for scvi_n200+imagenet_vit_l+multiprofile are exhausted. The image encoder (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) showed a large performance gap with pca_n2000 (~0.05-0.15), but it is untested whether scvi_n200's learned latent representations reduce dependence on the image encoder. Question: config_030 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) tests whether the strongest RNA encoder combined with the best aggregation and fusion can partially compensate for the weaker image encoder, potentially yielding a competitive and cheaper model. Rationale: As the final experiment, this is the highest-expected-accuracy untested configuration in the proven multiprofile+scvi_n200+transformer+weighted family. It is the most logical single-variable extension of the best result. If it approaches 0.70+, it would confirm a cheaper viable alternative; if it falls well below, it firmly establishes imagenet_vit_l as essential. Expected cost: moderate (~4-5 GPU hours), slightly less than config_045 since resnet50 is smaller than ViT-L, making it a reasonable final experiment within the remaining budget."
}

